0..70 Comment "// A monad relative to the shift `-F`: a unit returning a value and an"
71..143 Comment "// extension running a computation into a continuation, over a family of"
144..218 Comment "// computation types (Altenkirch, Chapman and Uustalu, _Monads need not be"
219..286 Comment "// endofunctors_, LMCS 11(1), 2015; Jiang, Xue and New, _Notions of"
287..360 Comment "// stack-manipulating computation and relative monads_, OOPSLA 2025). Its"
361..435 Comment "// host half is ordinary definitions: the option monad\'s two operations, a"
436..510 Comment "// program sequenced through them, and code polymorphic in the carrier. Of"
511..579 Comment "// the laws, the left unit is a second-order rule and the right unit"
580..644 Comment "// abstracts the variable the continuation binds; the twin holds"
645..695 Comment "// associativity, whose left side overlaps itself."
697..735 Comment "// `Maybe`, the option monad\'s values."
